 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "No ropes, staffs, snakes or sorcerers drawn. The sorcery is glossed as illusion («مجرد صنعة وخيال»). Light only when the truth prevails (117:7). STAGING v4: The gathering (As-Sa'di: on the day of the festival, people gathered in the forenoon, in front of a great crowd): an open town square by day (city setting; Egypt, no pyramids, no palms). The magicians are an uncountable group in dark robes (their number is not in the sources). c1 (113-115): they walk in (113:1) and speak to Pharaoh (113:4); a coins plate for the reward they ask (113:7, Al-Muyassar: a prize and money) and a crown plate for nearness to the king (114:3); Pharaoh answers (114:1). Musa (blue drop) comes in on 115:1 (As-Sa'di: when they were present with Musa), and is in the wide shot when he is named (115:2); the magicians speak to him (115:1). c2 (116-117): Musa says throw (116:1); the ropes, staffs and snakes are never drawn, and nothing appears or glows on the miracle words: the camera holds on the magicians (116:4, 116:10, 117:7) and on the uncountable crowd of onlookers whose eyes were bewitched (116:6, 117:10). 117:1-6 (the revelation to Musa, throw your staff) is held wide with his drop visible; no light plate (no light tied to a miracle word); the swallowing (117:7-11) is not drawn."
 },
